  "jsp": "JSP-000493",
  "erdos": 606,
  "title": "Which total numbers of determined lines are possible for a planar set of a prescribed number of points?",
  "scope": "For all sufficiently large n, a natural number m is the number of distinct affine lines determined by some n distinct points of the real plane if and only if ClassifiedValue n m holds. This is the explicit Erdos-Salamon union of low bands, a terminal interval, and the two terminal values choose(n,2)-2 and choose(n,2), with all band endpoints and exclusions printed in the audit. Both realization and impossibility directions are included; no classification for every small n or general-position assumption is claimed.",
  "attribution": "Existing plby formalization: Paul Erdos and Peter Salamon are credited for the mathematical classification; Codex and GPT-5.6 Sol for formalization. Imported Chapter39/Tucker files separately credit xiangyazi24/proof_in_the_book at commit 8ccc127c6c0109fa30ac61541420101376b24482 and retain their upstream compatibility notices. All selected source bytes and notices are preserved. This is verification evidence, not new-proof or first-formalization authorship.",
